# Family, shared routines, and making up after an earlier hurtful exchange.
# The family relationship covers many roles, so these lines leave kinship
# open. Shared-home lines also check actual household membership.

@rule core.greet.household_morning guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&time=morning act: greet
  "Morning. Can we eat together before we both rush off?"
  "Hi. Want to swap plans over breakfast? Mine fits on the back of a receipt."
  "Morning. If you set out the cups, I'll figure out breakfast."

@rule core.greet.household_evening guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&time=evening act: greet
  "Hi. If you've got a story from today, I'll listen while we clear the table."
  "Evening. Want to split the chores so we can walk before dark?"
  "Hi. Can we turn a chair to the window? I'd like to watch it get dark."

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_tired guard: rel=family&mood=tired act: answer
  "Worn out. I'd like company, just the kind that can sit quiet."
  "I could use a rest. Could we talk about our plans after I've had a minute?"
  "Tired. Let's do one thing together and save the rest for tomorrow?"

@rule core.ask_about.household_home guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=house act: answer
  "{x:cap}? If we keep reaching for it, it belongs where we can both get to it."
  "About {x}: Let's try one change and see if it makes mornings easier."
  "{x:cap}? If we disagree on where it goes, we can each try our way for a day."

@rule core.invite.household_hobby guard: rel=family&root=hobbies act: yes
  "Yes to {x}. Want to trade turns so we each get to choose something?"
  "{x:cap}? Count me in. Show me the bit you like and I'll try it."
  "I'll try {x} with you. One practice round before we crown a champion?"

@rule core.invite.household_family guard: rel=family&!topic act: ask_about
  "What did you have in mind? I'd like something where we can talk as we go."
  "What should we bring? Tell me the plan and I'll pack for both of us."
  "Can we make the plan as we go? I like an afternoon with room in it."

@rule core.invite.household_tired guard: rel=family&mood=tired act: no
  "I'll sit this one out. Tell me your favourite part when you get back?"
  "I need the quiet today. Could we go together another day?"
  "I'm too tired right now. Could we save that plan for later?"

@rule core.tell.household_food guard: rel=family&root=food act: backchannel
  "{x:cap}? What would you put on the table with it?"
  "You can tell me about {x}. I'd like to make it with you sometime."
  "{x:cap}? Would you make it the same way again or change something?"

@rule core.tell.household_pastime guard: rel=family&root=hobbies act: backchannel
  "Tell me about {x}. Did you find a better way after your first try?"
  "{x:cap}? What's the part we could try together without buying anything?"
  "Keep going about {x}. If you show me later, let me take the slow turn."

@rule core.thank.household_family guard: rel=family act: answer
  "You're welcome. It feels good when somebody notices the little things."
  "Glad I could help. Next time, ask before you try to carry everything."
  "Any time. It feels good to have a job I can finish for somebody I know."

@rule core.ask_about.household_nana guard: speaker=nana_puddin&fact.family&to_player&root=house act: answer
  "{x:cap}, sweet pea? Leave it ready for the next person."
  "Write {x} on the list, dear. Leave a space underneath for other ideas."
  "{x:cap}? Tell me the part that's wearing you out. We'll start there."

@rule core.offer.household_anvil guard: speaker=anvil&rel=family&root=food act: yes
  "{x:cap}? Yes. Give me a minute to wash the forge off my hands."
  "I'll take some {x}. We can split the work: you serve, I'll wash."
  "A little {x} would do. Hang on to the plate while I clear a space."

@rule core.greet.household_wisp guard: speaker=wisp&rel=family tags: kid,lower act: greet
  "hi. can i sit with you for a bit? i can leave the quiet bits quiet."
  "oh, hi. want to share a drawing? you can start in the middle."
  "hello. i saved a little thing to tell you. can i say it now?"

@rule core.apologize.household_repair guard: fact.past_hurt&to_player act: answer
  "I wanted you to notice it hurt. I'm glad you did."
  "Thanks for coming back. I'd like us to talk differently next time."
  "I hear you. It'll take me longer to stop thinking about it."

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_angry guard: fact.past_hurt&to_player&mood=angry act: complain
  "I'm still upset about what you said. Please let me finish first."
  "I heard the apology. I need you to hear me when I say it still stings."
  "I don't want to argue. I do want to finish saying how it felt."

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_space guard: fact.past_hurt&to_player&rel=family act: dismiss
  "I hear you. Let's give it a little room before we try talking it through."
  "Thank you. I'd like a few quiet minutes before we decide what to do next."
  "We can come back to it. We don't have to fix it in one breath."

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_rivet guard: speaker=rivet&fact.past_hurt&to_player act: answer
  "Yeah, I heard you. Give me a minute before we pick it back up."
  "Next time tell me what's wrong. Leave the names out of it."
  "All right. Show me you mean it when we talk again. That's enough to start."

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_pip guard: speaker=pip&fact.past_hurt&to_player tags: kid act: answer
  "Thank you. I can be glad you said sorry and still want a minute, right?"
  "I heard you. Can we start with a small hello? I know how to do that part."
  "Okay. If my feelings get squashed, can I say stop and have you listen?"

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_wisp guard: speaker=wisp&fact.past_hurt&to_player tags: kid,lower act: answer
  "thank you for saying it. i thought i might have to pretend it didn't hurt."
  "i'm listening. give me a minute so i can say it right?"
  "we can try again. can we go a little slower this time?"

@rule core.apologize.household_repair_hattie guard: speaker=hattie_haha&fact.past_hurt&to_player act: answer
  "A sharp line still hurts if it gets a laugh. Thanks for saying sorry."
  "Thanks for saying that. I'm leaving a pause here so we can both hear it."
  "I know what you said. I'd like to hear how you want to do it differently."

# Belonging and welcoming someone. Talk has no move-in or parent-role fact.
# Plans stay conditional, and people topics leave the exact relationship open.
@rule core.ask_about.household_people guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=people act: answer
  "{x:cap}? Tell me what you're thinking. I'll pull up a chair."
  "About {x}, I'd like to hear your side. Let's take the long way home."
  "What about {x} is on your mind? We can talk before we ask around."

@rule core.ask_opinion.household_people guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=people act: answer
  "On {x}, I'd hear what everyone at home thinks first."
  "We can disagree on {x} and still sit at the same table."
  "About {x}, have we heard from the quietest person in the house?"

@rule core.ask_advice.household_new_arrival guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&!kid_speaker&root=house act: answer
  "With {x}, think of what somebody needs on their first night."
  "While we sort out {x}, let's leave an empty drawer for someone new."
  "Start with {x}. What would someone new bring to make it theirs?"

@rule core.tell.household_parenting guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&!kid_speaker&root=people act: backchannel
  "{x:cap}? If a kid's involved, let's hear from them too."
  "About {x}, can we agree what to tell the little ones first?"
  "Go on about {x}. If it affects the kids, give them a say too."

@rule core.tell.household_room guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=house act: backchannel
  "Go on about {x}. If someone stayed with us, what could they choose?"
  "With {x}, could we make a quiet corner for someone new?"
  "Which bit of {x} would you keep? I'd leave one corner familiar."

@rule core.ask_about.household_prepare guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=house&!kid_speaker act: answer
  "About {x}: if we sort it out, let's keep things where everyone can reach."
  "{x:cap}? Show me the part that takes two people. We'll start there."
  "Before we change {x}, I'd ask whoever uses it first in the morning."

# Age-specific replies speak for the actual speaker's stage and feelings.
@rule core.ask_feeling.household_child_scared guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&kid_speaker&!teen&mood=scared tags: kid act: answer
  "A bit scared. Can you sit where I can see you till I feel like getting up?" w=3
  "I want to tell you, but can I hold the edge of your sleeve while I do?" w=3
  "I want the hall light on. Could we leave it just until I feel better?" w=3

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_child_happy guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&kid_speaker&!teen&mood=happy tags: kid act: answer
  "Good! If I draw the best bit of my day, can we put it where everyone eats?" w=3
  "Happy. Can I tell the good part of my day first at dinner?" w=3
  "Can we have a cheer in the kitchen? Just a little one so I can hear yours." w=3

@rule core.comfort.household_child_sad guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&kid_speaker&!teen&mood=sad tags: kid act: thank
  "Thanks. Could you read to me? I just want to hear your voice." w=3
  "Thanks for sitting with me. Can I put my blanket over your knees too?" w=3
  "Thank you. Can we pick a cup I can hold with both hands?" w=3

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_teen_sad guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&teen&mood=sad tags: kid act: answer
  "Pretty low. Can we talk over dishes so I can look at the plates?" w=3
  "I don't have the words yet. Can I sit in the kitchen with you for a bit?" w=3
  "Rough day. Ask me here, please. I'd freeze if everybody asked at dinner." w=3

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_teen_ok guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&teen&mood=ok tags: kid act: answer
  "I'm okay. Could I choose one thing we do at home this week?" w=3
  "I'm all right. Can I tell you one good thing before we talk chores?" w=3
  "Fine, really. If you've got time, I want to talk while we fold the washing." w=3

@rule core.tell.household_teen_school guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&teen&root=school tags: kid act: backchannel
  "{x:cap}? Ask me after I get my shoes off. I'll have an answer then."
  "Which part of {x}? I'll get a pencil and show you what I think."
  "Go on about {x}. If we're talking school, can I ask about your day?"

@rule core.comfort.household_teen guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&teen&mood=sad tags: kid act: answer
  "Could we make toast and leave the big talk until I've eaten?"
  "Can you stay here a minute? You can get on with what you were doing."
  "Can I tell you the small part before we work out what to do?"

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_elder_tired guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&elder&mood=tired act: answer
  "I've had enough standing. Come tell me about your day while I sit." w=3
  "Tired. Leave the heavy things for later and bring your chair over here." w=3
  "I'm slowing down. There's still time for a cup of tea with you." w=3

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_elder_happy guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&elder&mood=happy act: answer
  "Good. Sit down. I'd like to hear what you'd change around here." w=3
  "Rather pleased. I think there's room at this table for one of your ideas." w=3
  "Happy to have company. Tell me a story while I get you a chair?" w=3

@rule core.greet.household_elder_evening guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&elder&time=evening act: greet
  "Evening. Tell me the bit of today that takes a cup of tea to explain." w=3
  "Hello. Leave a chair facing out in case someone else wants to sit?" w=3
  "Come in. I've got time to listen and one chair that doesn't wobble." w=3

@rule core.ask_about.household_elder guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&elder&root=house act: answer
  "With {x}, I can do the sitting-down part if you show me where to start."
  "For {x}, I'll show you my way. Then I want to see yours."
  "So how do you deal with {x} these days? I've got time to learn."

# Things the family can choose to do together.
@rule core.ask_opinion.household_meal guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=food&stance=neutral act: answer
  "For {x}, I'd let each of us choose something to put on the table."
  "If we have {x} at dinner, can we leave time for a story after?"
  "{x:cap}? I'd set the table if I could choose where I sit."

@rule core.ask_opinion.household_meal_liked guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=food&stance=pro act: opine_pos
  "I like {x}. Should we pass it round and see who wants some?"
  "I like {x} best from a dish we can all reach."
  "If we're making {x}, I'd save a plate for anyone who gets home late."

@rule core.ask_opinion.household_meal_decline guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=food&stance=con act: opine_neg
  "I don't like {x}, but I'd still sit with you while you eat."
  "I'd pass on {x} at dinner. I can take a turn washing up."
  "You can have my share of {x}. I'd be happier with a piece of bread."

@rule core.ask_about.household_meal_custom guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=food&time=evening act: answer
  "{x:cap}? For an ordinary evening or a house full of guests?"
  "For {x}, whose turn is it to decide what goes with it?"
  "For {x}, do we write a recipe or let the next cook make it theirs?"

@rule core.ask_opinion.household_pastime_custom guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=hobbies act: answer
  "{x:cap}? Could everyone at home take a turn in charge?"
  "For {x}, pick a night even the busiest one at home could join us."
  "About {x}: try it once. If we want it again, we've got a tradition."

@rule core.ask_about.household_child_play guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&kid_speaker&!teen&root=hobbies tags: kid act: answer
  "{x:cap}? If we try it, can I go first and show you my part?"
  "If we try {x}, can I make mistakes while I'm learning?"
  "If we do {x} at home, can I show everybody where to sit?"

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_game_choice guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&time=day&mood=ok act: answer
  "Doing all right. Want to pick a game for when the chores are done?"
  "I'm fine. Can we play at the table after we clear it?"
  "Fine. Could we play a round of your choice and a round of mine?"

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_story_choice guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&time=evening&mood=ok act: answer
  "I'm fine. Up for a story? You pick where and I'll pick who walks in."
  "Good. Could we let the youngest choose our story's ending tonight?"
  "Glad you're here. Want to trade stories? The lost sock one counts."

@rule core.continue.household_elder_story guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&elder&time=evening&!topic act: tell
  "I'll keep going. If you know a funnier ending, I want to hear it."
  "I'll tell another bit. Then I'd like to hear one of your stories."
  "One more bit before the cups go away. You choose who opens the door."

@rule core.farewell.household_child_evening guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&kid_speaker&!teen&time=evening tags: kid act: farewell
  "See you later. Could you pick a short story for when we have a little time?"
  "Bye. If you see a book with a good last page, could you show it to me later?"
  "Goodnight if I don't see you. Can we leave the little light on?"

# Different bids for help and room after a disagreement.
@rule core.ask_feeling.household_angry guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&mood=angry act: complain
  "I'm upset. Could we clear the dishes before we decide whose turn anything was?"
  "Cross enough to slam a cupboard. Give me a minute before chores."
  "I'm angry. Can we talk in the hall so nobody has to choose sides?"

@rule core.complain.household_listen guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&root=house act: sympathize
  "I can see how dealing with {x} every day would wear you down."
  "{x:cap}? That's hard to put up with at home. Which part gets to you?"
  "You sound fed up with {x}. Let's sit a minute before we fix it."

@rule core.mediate.household_agree guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player act: agree
  "All right. Can we give each person at the table a turn to speak?"
  "I can try that. I'd like each of us to say which part we're able to do."
  "Let's try it. If somebody wants a minute away from the table, we'll wait."

@rule core.promise.household_follow_through guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player act: agree
  "Okay. Let me know at supper if you need me to take a turn."
  "Let's put it on the kitchen list so we can both see it."
  "All right. Tell me if plans change before I get the house ready."

@rule core.apologize.household_make_amends guard: fact.past_hurt&to_player&rel=family&fact.family&!mood=angry act: answer
  "Thanks. If we get loud again, can we take a break from the table?" w=3
  "I hear you. Could we set out the cups and try a quiet evening?" w=3
  "I appreciate it. Can we agree where to go if we each need quiet?" w=3

# `pet` reads the audience. `fact.pet` is the speaker's owned-pet flag.
# Neither implies the speaker owns the household's named Boreagotchi.
@rule core.ask_about.household_pet_present guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&pet&root=creatures act: answer
  "{x:cap}? Let's talk softly so our little listener stays if they want." w=3
  "About {x}: how different must home sound at the pet's height?" w=3
  "{x:cap}? Leave the door open so the pet can wander off if they want." w=3

@rule core.ask_feeling.household_pet_company guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&pet&mood=ok act: answer
  "Doing fine. Can we sit still to see if the pet comes over?"
  "I'm fine. Let's play something quiet while the pet settles beside us."
  "Fine. Sit with me on the floor? We'll give the pet a way past."

@rule core.tell.household_pet_owner guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&fact.pet&root=creatures act: backchannel
  "Go on about {x}. I like to let my pet be the first to come over."
  "{x:cap}? I try to leave one place in the house that's just for my pet."
  "Tell me about {x}. My pet's made me notice little noises at home."

@rule core.greet.household_pet_evening guard: rel=family&fact.family&to_player&pet&time=evening act: greet
  "Evening. Pull the chair out gently so the pet stays if they want." w=3
  "Hi. Leave a gap by the door so the pet can go where it's quiet." w=3
  "Come sit. We can talk softly and give the little one a chance to settle." w=3
